{
  "description": "Futures WebSocket channels (server 6919535). Binding client rules: (1) the six futures event types below and futures.resync are known event types, delivered as events with type, channel, sequence and data (never dropped as unknown); (2) channel-name helpers build futures.mids, futures.orderbook:{coin}, futures.trades:{coin}, futures.candles:{coin}:{interval}, futures.status and futures.account; the coin is sent exactly as given (case-sensitive, ASCII letters/digits, 1-20 chars) and the interval must be one of 1m 5m 15m 1h 4h 1d, else a local CONFIG error with nothing sent; (3) futures.account is a private channel: held until auth/auth_key succeeds, like the other private channels; (4) futures.resync on a public futures channel is delivered as an event plus a resync notification for that channel (refetch over REST), with no resubscribe; (5) futures.resync on futures.account is delivered the same way AND the client automatically sends unsubscribe then subscribe for futures.account (the server's poller stopped; re-subscribing alone is a no-op); a refusal of that subscribe (e.g. NOT_FOUND 'No futures account') is reported as an error and the channel is no longer held; (6) a refused futures subscribe (RATE_LIMITED, NOT_FOUND, VALIDATION_FAILED, SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE) is reported and NOT retried automatically: WS error frames carry no retry_after; (7) no snapshot arrives on subscribe for public futures channels: seed from REST; (8) book levels are {price,size} objects, not [price,quantity] arrays; book, mids, positions and orders frames are full replacements; (9) the client sends a ping at least every 60 s (the server closes connections silent for 90-120 s). Sequences: public futures channels are not gap-tracked (full replacements or unrecoverable); futures.account restarts its sequence after a resubscribe.",
